# Scan Kit 2

Follow [docs/software/architecture.md](docs/software/architecture.md) and [docs/software/software-development-plan.md](docs/software/software-development-plan.md).

- Domain behavior lives in `scan-kit-core` once. Session files and the sqlite store live in `scan-kit-io`. GPU work uses `wgpu` only. Plot drawing lives in `scan-kit-plot`, which also builds to wasm32 for the webview. Do not draw plots in TypeScript or ship frames over the Tauri bridge. Compute kernels live in `scan-kit-compute`. Register each operation on that crate's tool catalog. `scan-kit-mcp` and Tauri commands call that function. They do not reimplement it.
- Workflow tools call granular functions in process.
- Do not add a PyO3 bridge or a second Python implementation of ported behavior.
- A port deletes, in the same change, the Python modules and tests that exist only for that capability. Leave a module that unported code still imports. Files still under `scan_kit/` or `tests/` are unported. Phase 1 itself does not delete product Python.
- Desktop chrome stays on the stock shadcn dark theme from [ui.shadcn.com](https://ui.shadcn.com/) (`base-nova`, Base UI). Tabular data uses Glide Data Grid, themed from the stock tokens. Add chrome with `npx shadcn add <name>` in `apps/desktop` and use that file as written. Do not hand-write a select, input, button, checkbox, dialog, menu, tabs, or label, and do not restyle a copied component. Do not edit theme tokens, add custom color, radius, type, or spacing CSS, or add another component library for chrome. Do not add a shadcn Table for data.
- Pull requests target `develop`. Do not bump `scan_kit/__init__.py` to match the Rust `2.0.0-dev` workspace version.
- A new direct dependency updates [docs/software/soup.md](docs/software/soup.md) in the same change.
